      "assertedBy": "agent/analystos-ci",
      "visibility": "public",
      "detail": "analystos/l2/analyze.py: analyze_document now catches\nanthropic.APIError (the common base for every SDK-raised failure - a\nhit spend limit, a bad/revoked key, a rate limit, an outage) around\nthe one API call and re-raises as a clean ValueError, never echoing\nthe raw exception. Without this, any of those failures would have\npassed through api/analyze.py's ValueError-only except block\nuncaught, surfacing as a raw, unhandled 500 instead of the same clean\n{\"error\": \"...\"} shape every other pipeline failure already gets.\nPrompted directly by setting up a real ANTHROPIC_API_KEY and a\nmonthly spend cap - hitting that cap needed to fail the same honest\nway as everything else.\n\nTests added at both layers (analyze_document directly, and through\nthe Flask route) using a real anthropic.APIConnectionError raised\nfrom a mocked client - still no real API call, no cost.\n\nROADMAP.md: reconciled through Slice 26 - it previously stopped at\nSlice 24. Adds Slice 25 (universal upload) and Slice 26 (narrated\nanalysis) under a new \"Beyond the original MVP\" heading, since both\nwent past what the tracked phase originally scoped.",
